<title>FRANCE: Striking French fishermen invited for talks.</title>
<headline>Striking French fishermen invited for talks.</headline>
<dateline>LILLE, France 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Agriculture Minister Philippe Vasseur has called on striking French fishermen blocking several Channel ports to meet him for talks to settle their dispute, officials said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Vasseur told officials of the fishermens' unions he was ready to receive them &quot;when they wanted to settle this affair&quot; and suggested a meeting in Paris at 10.00 a.m. (0800 GMT) on Thursday, the officials said.</p>
<p>The blockade by the fishermen's boats, which began on Tuesday, has crippled traffic to and from Dunkirk, Calais and Boulogne.</p>
<p>Hundreds of trucks were backed up on a motorway near the British port of Dover because of the blockade while thousands of travellers faced delays as ferries were diverted to the Belgian port of Zeebrugge.</p>
<p>The fishermen's protest is over European Union regulations calling for larger holes in the mesh of the fishermens' nets.</p>
</text>
